@startuml
title Launch Manager - Control Interface Startup

autonumber "<b>[00]"

participant "StateManager" as sm
participant "Launch Manager" as LM
participant "OS (kernel)" as kernel
participant "setup_filesystems.sh" as fs

activate LM

note over sm,LM
Launch Manager activates its initial Run Target "Minimal", which requires StateManager.
StateManager depends on setup_filesystems.sh, so it is started first.
end note

group #White Start setup_filesystems.sh
    LM -> kernel : Start setup_filesystems.sh
    kernel -> fs ++ : Start setup_filesystems.sh
    LM -> LM : Wait for setup_filesystems.sh ready condition
    fs -> kernel : exit
    destroy fs
    kernel -> LM : setup_filesystems.sh terminated successfully
    LM -> LM : Component setup_filesystems.sh Ready
end group

LM -> kernel : start StateManager

kernel -> sm : start
activate sm

...

sm -> LM: RegisterActivationCallback(callback)


note over sm,LM
The transition to Run Target "Minimal" is still ongoing, no Run Target is active yet.
end note
sm -> LM : GetActiveRunTarget
sm <-- LM: In Transition

sm -> LM : Report Running via Lifecycle API

...

sm <-- LM: Invoke callback: Run Target "Minimal" successfully activated due to Initial Startup

note over sm,LM
The transition to Run Target "Minimal" has finished, and it is now the active Run Target.
end note
sm -> LM : GetActiveRunTarget
sm <-- LM: Minimal


...
@enduml
